<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">9 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 9 August, from 48 BCE to 1974.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/pompey" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pompey.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/48-bce">48 BCE</a> <span class="tih-ago">2,073 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Caesar defeats Pompey at Pharsalus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>'s veterans routed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a>'s larger army in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaly">Thessaly</a>. Pompey fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, where he was murdered, and Caesar became master of the Roman world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/378">378 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,648 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Goths destroy a Roman army and kill Emperor Valens at Adrianople</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Gothic cavalry and infantry overwhelmed the Eastern Roman army near Adrianople in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>, killing Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valens">Valens</a> and much of his force. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> was never again able to expel the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goths">Goths</a> from its territory.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valens">Valens</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1173">1173 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">853 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Construction begins on the bell tower of Pisa</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Work started on the campanile of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisa">Pisa</a> Cathedral. Soft ground made it lean by the time the third storey was built, and it became famous as the Leaning Tower of Pisa.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1329">1329 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">697 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope John XXII creates the Diocese of Quilon in India</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-john-xxii">Pope John XXII</a>, the second of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avignon">Avignon</a> popes, created a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> diocese at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kollam">Quilon</a>, in present-day Kollam in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and appointed the French-born Jordanus as its first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-john-xxii">Pope John XXII</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1638">1638 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">388 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bernhard of Saxe-Weimar defeats imperial troops at Wittenweiher</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near the village of Wittenweiher, now part of Schwanau in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, an army under the Protestant general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernhard-of-saxe-weimar">Bernhard of Saxe-Weimar</a> defeated imperial troops in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War. The village was destroyed in the battle.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernhard-of-saxe-weimar">Bernhard of Saxe-Weimar</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US bomber drops an atomic bomb on Nagasaki</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The plutonium bomb Fat Man exploded over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagasaki">Nagasaki</a>, killing some 40,000 people at once and many more later. Six days later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> announced its surrender.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagasaki">Nagasaki</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1969">1969 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">57 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Manson Family members murder Sharon Tate and four others</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Followers of Charles Manson killed actress Sharon Tate, who was heavily pregnant, and four others at her <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/los-angeles">Los Angeles</a> home. The murders horrified America and Manson became a byword for evil.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1974">1974 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">52 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gerald Ford becomes president after Nixon resigns</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Gerald Ford was sworn in as the 38th president, telling Americans 'our long national nightmare is over'. His pardon of Nixon a month later probably cost him the 1976 election.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 9 August <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-de-braose-4th-lord-of-bramber"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-de-braose-4th-lord-of-bramber.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William de Braose, 4th Lord of Bramber</span><span class="tp">c. 1144–1211</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hermann-hesse"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hermann-hesse.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hermann Hesse</span><span class="tp">1877–1962</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/dmitri-shostakovich"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Dmitri Shostakovich</span><span class="tp">1906–1975</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
